# 🤖 B2B PET Bottle Review Intelligence System

An AI-powered **B2B customer review intelligence system** developed as part of an AI Problem Design Internship Task at **Swynex Technologies**.

The system uses **Natural Language Processing (NLP)** and machine learning to automatically analyze client reviews, identify sentiment, classify feedback, and flag potentially suspicious or biased reviews for further manual verification.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

Swynex Technologies receives a large volume of B2B client feedback through its order and communication channels.

Manually reviewing hundreds of client reviews can be:

* ⏳ Time-consuming
* 📉 Inconsistent
* 👀 Prone to missing emerging negative trends
* 🔍 Difficult to monitor at scale

This project proposes an AI-based solution that converts unstructured client feedback into **structured and actionable business insights**.

### The system is designed to:

* Detect **Positive / Negative sentiment**
* Analyze different types of client feedback
* Identify potentially **fake or biased reviews**
* Generate business-level review insights
* Provide outputs that can support quality and customer-experience decisions

---

## 🎯 Problem Statement

> **How can AI automatically analyze large volumes of B2B customer reviews and help business teams identify customer sentiment and potentially suspicious feedback without manually reading every review?**

The objective is to build a lightweight machine-learning solution that can process text-based feedback efficiently on a local machine without requiring a dedicated GPU.

---

## 👥 Target Users

| User                        | Purpose                                                       |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Business Analytics Team** | Analyze customer sentiment and identify trends                |
| **Quality Manager**         | Monitor negative feedback and potential quality issues        |
| **Business Team**           | Use review insights for operational decision-making           |
| **B2B Clients**             | Their feedback contributes to product and process improvement |

