This type of analysis can help business teams quickly understand the overall customer-feedback distribution without manually reviewing every record.

---

## 📊 Model Performance

The current experiment produced:

| Metric             |   Result | Target |
| ------------------ | -------: | -----: |
| Accuracy           | **100%** |   >85% |
| Weighted Precision | **1.00** |   >85% |
| Weighted Recall    | **1.00** |   >85% |
| Weighted F1-Score  | **1.00** |   >85% |

### ⚠️ Validation Note

The reported 100% performance should be **validated carefully before being treated as a final production metric**.

A perfect score on a dataset of approximately 500 records can sometimes indicate:

* Data leakage
* Duplicate or near-duplicate records across train/test sets
* An overly small test set
* A very clean or easily separable dataset

For a production-ready evaluation, the model should be tested using a properly separated and **stratified train/test split**, with duplicate or near-duplicate reviews checked to prevent leakage.

Therefore, the 100% result is reported as the **current experimental result**, not as a guarantee of real-world performance.

